# ble.sh settings (https://github.com/akinomyoga/ble.sh), read when .bashrc sources ble.sh.
# Linked to ~/.blerc by setup.bash. Everything not mentioned here is a ble.sh default.
#
# Inline suggestions (zsh-autosuggestions counterpart) are on by default and come from the
# history. Default keys, kept as they are because they match the PowerShell profile
# (PSReadLine ForwardChar / ForwardWord) and zsh:
#   C-f / right / end   insert the whole suggestion (cursor at end of line)
#   M-f / C-right       insert the next word only
#   S-RET               insert the whole suggestion from anywhere
#   C-RET               insert it and run the line
# .inputrc is read by ble.sh too, so C-p / C-n / up / down stay history-search-backward /
# -forward and M-k / M-j stay menu-complete, as in plain readline.

# Share history between sessions the ble.sh way. .bashrc skips its
# `history -a; history -c; history -r` PROMPT_COMMAND hack when ble.sh is loaded: with
# ble.sh that hack makes it reload the whole history file at every prompt.
bleopt history_share=1
